{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1554585-npc-ideas-exalted-playstyles","id":1554585,"title":"Npc ideas--Exalted playstyles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Alchemical Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-10-22T21:00:26-07:00","id":1554585,"title":"Npc ideas--Exalted playstyles","content":"So, in coming up with the Alchemical NPCs/pregens that will be involved in my local Autocthonian setting, I had a quirky idea that I am having trouble fleshing out. I definitely know that Charms and Submodules will be needed, but I am having trouble parsing through the ones I might need to portray them in the way I want. The general gist of it is that I sort of want to make an Alchemical equivalent of the PLAYSTYLE of each caste's Creation counterpart, with a slight scifi bent. Hopefully my request will sort of make more sense in the context of each Caste, and those who know the Charms better than I can help me figure out how to make them work.<br /> <br /> For the Orichalcum, I wanted to mimic the playstyle of a Solar--A champion who can change the world easily, accidentally even, but must hide their power for fear of being discovered and hunted. In my head, I especially remember movies like DARYL, Fifth Element, or even Stranger Things. Imagine an Alchemical who woke up and his memories and duties overwhelmed him. He used his power to escape his facility and try to hide. I am even sort of leaning into the idea that designer of his body made him as human as possible, and that he is now trying to hide amongst the Nuradi peoples, pretending to be a teenage non-alchemical and hoping his family doesnt turn him in to the government. Clearly, he will need Charms to hide his Alchemical nature and masquerade as a normal human boy.<br /> <br /> The Moonsilver is far easier to design. The concept behind her is that the Gateway people somehow managed to figure out how to make an Alchemical. She isn't QUITE a voidbringer, but she doesn't trust the Tripartite.<br /> <br /> Jade is a other tough one, to replicate the Dragon Blooded experience. Due to dynasties and bloodlines being a no-no in much of Autocthonia, I imagine he was a BIT of a secret project. His soul the culmination of lifetimes of privelage and power, his body expertly designed, his wealth and status built up for him to be available the moment he opened his eyes. While the Jade tend to be working class heroes, I see him as more of an ultra-manager, a brilliant financier and social genius akin to Jobs and Luthor. If Dragon Blooded are princes, he is an Exalted CEO/CFO backed by centuries of conspiracy and money.<br /> <br /> For Starmetal, thats pretty easy. Machine Saint, religious and metaphysical, almost literally an Angel from D:tD.<br /> <br /> For Soulsteel, that one is also pretty hard. Abyssals are the dark darklings of the Underworld and its dead gods. I kinda think an angle of history and memory, like a CofD Mummy, with a hint of vampiric parasitism? Plus actual state support, perhaps from a rogue group in Nurad that is experimenting with Gremlinism to prepare for the Blight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T11:01:03-07:00","id":1554734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1554585-npc-ideas-exalted-playstyles#post1554585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Starmetal, thats pretty easy. Machine Saint, religious and metaphysical, almost literally an Angel from D:tD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally what the Adamant caste's shtick is now. Starmetal is more like the seers in Minority Report, but conscious and walking around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T21:13:16-08:00","id":1557752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/alchemical-exalted/1554585-npc-ideas-exalted-playstyles?p=1554734#post1554734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Literally what the Adamant caste's shtick is now. Starmetal is more like the seers in Minority Report, but conscious and walking around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically true as is, yes. But this particular batch of Alchemicals is meant to mimic their Creation-born counterparts deliberately, as a twist. Hence why the Starmetal Caste is meant to be a secret, wise weaver of destiny, emissary of the machine gods, stranger, and mystery. Meanwhile, the Adamant Caste has more of the Auroral flavor--She is an international performance artist. Think Sharon Apple of Macross meets Taylor Swift and Jem. <br /> <br /> The Starmetal will even eventually get that Charm that makes others forget meeting them, like a Sidereal. The Adamant focuses a lot on social charms to sway her fans, like a Hearteater. <br /> <br /> Ive developed the ideas a bit further, and it has taken some finesse and wiggling to portray them right. But as of now, the Orichalcum appears as a 15 year old, has adopted a small family to serve as his parents, and works at a fast food joint, trying his best to avoid notice. He doesnt have to hide from a Wyld Hunt, so instead, he hides from the Tripartite and the Nuradi government because reasons, and has gone out of his way to not reveal his Exalted nature. The Jade caste is as rich and influential as a Realm Dynast, having been a secret project of a Hereditary Cult and Soulgem favoritism, now a sort of Steve Jobs or Elon Musk. <br /> <br /> The whole idea for these NPCs is sort of an example to my players that its possible to play &quot;Exalted Modern/Cyberpunk/80s sci fi&quot; with Autocthonia. So I deliberately wanted &quot;the same Exalted you know, but Autocthonian&quot;. <br /> <br /> Granted, its not like these ideas translate perfectly. Indeed, the Metropolis of my setting is VERY unique and custom tailored for any of it to work. Most, especially the Orichalcum wouldn't work without some setting specific quirks. For example, the Orichalcum &quot;Solar&quot; can only hide easily because the Metropolis has extensive migrant work from Gateway Folk, and thus a lack of Populat Soulgem wasn't a huge issue in getting a job. Immigrant Gateway Folk and occasional gemless families are part of the local economy and are only recently facing scrutiny from officials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T14:18:22-08:00","id":1557788,"title":"","content":"Have you considered making the Solar-alike Orichalcum an Apostate? Grand and unusual powers whose source and visual manifestation needs to be rigorously guarded to avoid society-wide hatred and assault, prone to terrible behavior if Limit isn't carefully managed... If you're willing to draw from 2e, they even had a unique power for keeping and swapping between a Charm panoply without institutional support that's quite helpful for staying in hiding, you could adapt that to 3e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28948-mj6373","name":"MJ6373","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}